HyperFrames: https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes
  Copyright HeyGen. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).
  raea's HTML composition path ports from HyperFrames' packages/core and packages/producer: the composition format,
  the compile rules for sub-compositions (inlining, CSS and script scoping, inner-root wrappers), the runtime timing
  rules (data-start expressions, clip visibility, frame snapping, timeline nesting, variables) and the deterministic
  font rules. The ported files carry a header saying so: sdk/ui/src/html.ts and sdk/ui/src/html/compile.ts, fonts.ts
  and runtime.ts. raea renamed the format's runtime names (window.__raea, data-raea-* attributes, the "html" profile).

muxide: vendor/muxide, MIT OR Apache-2.0 (its LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).

animato (MIT OR Apache-2.0), usvg and resvg (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), mediabunny (MPL-2.0, used unmodified), manifold-rust
(Apache-2.0), Bevy (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and the other crates and packages in each Cargo.lock and package.json, each under its own licence.

The Windows build (docs/ports.feature PT20) adds: junction 1.4.2 (MIT, node_modules' links in io/npm) and windows-sys
0.61.2 (Microsoft, MIT OR Apache-2.0, in io/trace); every build has dunce 1.0.5 (CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0 OR Apache-2.0, plain
paths for Windows in runtime/bundle). It ships none of Microsoft's C runtime or SDK files: the runtime comes from the
Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable, installed on the machine.
The native target (engine/rune, docs/targets.feature) builds on Rune (https://github.com/anomalyco/rune, Copyright
2026 Anomaly, MIT; LICENSES/rune-0.0.1/repository-LICENSE): rune, rune-kit and their crates, by a pinned rev.

